337
01:02:09.586 --> 01:02:10.586
almost forgotten.

338
01:02:11.586 --> 01:02:13.586
I don't want to rush over that, do you understand what I mean?

339
01:02:14.586 --> 01:02:15.586
And we have all the time.

340
01:02:16.586 --> 01:02:18.586
And so today I want to give a resurrection sermon.

341
01:02:19.586 --> 01:02:22.586
I want to give a sermon today about the death of Jesus.

342
01:02:23.586 --> 01:02:24.586
And about the resurrection.

343
01:02:24.586 --> 01:02:26.586
And about the transformation of feeling.

344
01:02:27.586 --> 01:02:29.586
If that is alright with you.

345
01:02:30.586 --> 01:02:32.586
And it can be found in the last chapter of the gospel.

346
01:02:33.586 --> 01:02:35.586
For the last chapter of the gospel, every time...

347
01:02:36.586 --> 01:02:39.586
is about the climax of what has happened.

348
01:02:40.586 --> 01:02:41.586
Namely the death of Jesus.

349
01:02:42.586 --> 01:02:43.586
On a cross.

350
01:02:44.586 --> 01:02:45.586
And his resurrection.

351
01:02:46.586 --> 01:02:49.586
And I will read with you Luke chapter 24.

352
01:02:50.586 --> 01:02:52.586
And it is a powerful story.

353
01:02:53.586 --> 01:02:54.586
And it is...

354
01:02:55.586 --> 01:02:57.586
I actually don't know what the title is in Dutch.

355
01:02:58.586 --> 01:03:02.586
But it is about the two men who are on their way to Emmaus.

356
01:03:03.586 --> 01:03:05.586
Emmaus. Emmaus, Emmaus.

357
01:03:07.586 --> 01:03:09.586
And this is an amazing story.

358
01:03:10.586 --> 01:03:11.586
You should never...

359
01:03:12.586 --> 01:03:13.586
Especially not with Luke, by the way.

360
01:03:14.586 --> 01:03:18.586
For he was truly a master in writing stories.

361
01:03:18.586 --> 01:03:20.586
In which almost every word had a meaning.

362
01:03:21.586 --> 01:03:22.586
It is really...

363
01:03:23.586 --> 01:03:24.586
Luke was next level.

364
01:03:25.586 --> 01:03:26.586
That was really amazing.

365
01:03:27.586 --> 01:03:29.586
And I want to go through the story with you.

366
01:03:30.586 --> 01:03:31.586
Exegetical.

367
01:03:32.586 --> 01:03:34.586
That means that you go through the text.

368
01:03:35.586 --> 01:03:38.586
And that you pause at a few words each time and talk about them for a moment.

369
01:03:39.586 --> 01:03:41.586
To explain how deep this story is.

370
01:03:42.586 --> 01:03:45.586
Because this story is deeper than just a side story.

371
01:03:45.586 --> 01:03:46.586
The story is...

372
01:03:47.586 --> 01:03:50.586
Realtime for you and for me today.

373
01:03:51.586 --> 01:03:52.586
So...

374
01:03:53.586 --> 01:03:54.586
Let's give it a go.

375
01:03:55.586 --> 01:03:58.586
Luke chapter 24, verses 13 to 33.

376
01:03:59.586 --> 01:04:01.586
Two of the disciples...

377
01:04:03.586 --> 01:04:04.586
Were on their way that day...

378
01:04:06.586 --> 01:04:07.586
To the village of Emmaus.

379
01:04:08.586 --> 01:04:11.586
That is 60 stadia, which is about 18 kilometers from Jerusalem.

380
01:04:11.586 --> 01:04:14.586
On the way, they talked to each other about everything that had happened.

381
01:04:16.586 --> 01:04:21.586
While they were walking and talking about this, Jesus himself came to them.

382
01:04:24.586 --> 01:04:29.586
While they were talking about everything that had happened over the past weekend,

383
01:04:30.586 --> 01:04:32.586
Jesus himself came to them.

384
01:04:34.586 --> 01:04:36.586
This is already amazing in itself.

385
01:04:36.586 --> 01:04:44.586
For I want to tell you in 2023, Jesus is still the one who walks with you in this life.

386
01:04:46.586 --> 01:04:48.586
Jesus is such a good giver.

387
01:04:49.586 --> 01:04:50.586
He is so loving.

388
01:04:51.586 --> 01:05:00.586
He is so amazing that he does not want you or me to walk away in conflict.

389
01:05:00.586 --> 01:05:03.586
He does not want us to stray from the path.

390
01:05:04.586 --> 01:05:07.586
He does not want us to lose heart.

391
01:05:08.586 --> 01:05:10.586
Can you imagine what is happening here?

392
01:05:11.586 --> 01:05:21.586
Here you have Jesus, the Almighty, the great God of the universe,

393
01:05:22.586 --> 01:05:25.586
who is concerned with everything that has happened.

394
01:05:25.586 --> 01:05:33.586
The great God of the universe, who is working on his grand plan.

395
01:05:35.586 --> 01:05:41.586
And this plan was already fully known and written out before the world existed.

396
01:05:42.586 --> 01:05:48.586
When God the Father, the architect of everything that exists, laid out his plan

397
01:05:48.586 --> 01:05:53.586
for what is currently unfolding and what happened 2000 years ago,

398
01:05:54.586 --> 01:05:59.586
then Jesus decided this whole plan together with the Father.

399
01:06:00.586 --> 01:06:07.586
And this is such a great plan, for billions of people are included in this grand plan.

400
01:06:07.586 --> 01:06:13.586
I would almost say that you would say, here comes the grand plan, everyone and everything aside.

401
01:06:13.586 --> 01:06:17.586
But instead, Jesus says to little children, let them come to me.

402
01:06:17.586 --> 01:06:21.586
He is so detailed. He is so loving.

403
01:06:21.586 --> 01:06:25.586
And you must see this here, what Luke is writing here,

404
01:06:25.586 --> 01:06:33.586
is that it says and Jesus himself came walking with two men who were actually lost.

405
01:06:34.586 --> 01:06:41.586
For this story, namely, is a story that does not have a positive light when it comes to these two men.

406
01:06:42.586 --> 01:06:46.586
These two men had lost their way. These two men were not happy.

407
01:06:46.586 --> 01:06:50.586
These two men were actually walking the wrong way.

408
01:06:51.586 --> 01:06:55.586
This is not a good story as these two men are doing.

409
01:06:56.586 --> 01:06:58.586
I must tell you something else.

410
01:06:58.586 --> 01:07:08.586
Jerusalem was the place where all of Scripture already knew that Jerusalem was the place of the climax.

411
01:07:08.586 --> 01:07:12.586
Jerusalem was the place where God would restore things.

412
01:07:12.586 --> 01:07:15.586
Jerusalem was the holy city. Jerusalem is the city of promises.

413
01:07:15.586 --> 01:07:18.586
Jerusalem is the place.

414
01:07:19.586 --> 01:07:27.586
And so when the Bible says here that two men are walking the road to Emmaus away from Jerusalem,

415
01:07:27.586 --> 01:07:29.586
there is already symbolism in that.

416
01:07:29.586 --> 01:07:33.586
It means that these two men should have actually stayed in Jerusalem.

417
01:07:33.586 --> 01:07:40.586
They should have stayed in the place of promise, but instead, they are walking away from Jerusalem.

418
01:07:40.586 --> 01:07:41.586
That is how you should read this.

419
01:07:41.586 --> 01:07:45.586
It is not just a boring detail to say, oh that is 18 kilometers from Jerusalem.

420
01:07:45.586 --> 01:07:47.586
Who cares?

421
01:07:47.586 --> 01:07:53.586
But what it does mean is that Jerusalem is a significant city.

422
01:07:53.586 --> 01:08:00.586
The place of the mountain where Jesus died for your and my sins and where He rose again.

423
01:08:00.586 --> 01:08:03.586
So Jerusalem is the place.

424
01:08:03.586 --> 01:08:07.586
Is the place where these two men should have stayed.

425
01:08:07.586 --> 01:08:09.586
They should have stayed there with the disciples.

426
01:08:09.586 --> 01:08:10.586
They should have been in prayer.

427
01:08:10.586 --> 01:08:15.586
They should have rejoiced, for there had already been women who said that Jesus had risen.

428
01:08:15.586 --> 01:08:20.586
This is the place where they should have stayed as Jesus had said.

429
01:08:20.586 --> 01:08:25.586
But instead, they are walking away to Emmaus.

430
01:08:25.586 --> 01:08:28.586
This is not a good story.

431
01:08:28.586 --> 01:08:34.586
And then it is so beautiful to realize that we have a Lord.

432
01:08:34.586 --> 01:08:39.586
Who rises so powerfully and mightily from the dead.

433
01:08:39.586 --> 01:08:42.586
This is nuclear what is happening here.

434
01:08:42.586 --> 01:08:44.586
Jesus rises from the dead.

435
01:08:44.586 --> 01:08:46.586
The Almighty.

436
01:08:46.586 --> 01:08:53.586
And He takes the time to seek out two boys Himself.

437
01:08:53.586 --> 01:08:58.586
Who seem to be lost in the grand plan that is unfolding.

438
01:08:58.586 --> 01:09:02.586
God loves you.

439
01:09:02.586 --> 01:09:05.586
Jesus is a person.

440
01:09:05.586 --> 01:09:08.586
And He walks with you through life.

441
01:09:08.586 --> 01:09:14.586
And when you go astray, He is eager to walk beside you.

442
01:09:14.586 --> 01:09:19.586
To walk with you through that struggle.

443
01:09:19.586 --> 01:09:25.586
Make mistakes in your life, Jesus is right there.

444
01:09:25.586 --> 01:09:31.586
Are you thinking wrongly, Jesus is right there.

445
01:09:31.586 --> 01:09:40.586
If you walk away from Him, He is already there where you plan to go.

446
01:09:40.586 --> 01:09:42.586
Hi!

447
01:09:42.586 --> 01:09:46.586
But not to reject you.

448
01:09:46.586 --> 01:09:50.586
But to bring you back to Jerusalem.

449
01:09:50.586 --> 01:09:53.586
To bring you back to His congregation.

450
01:09:53.586 --> 01:10:00.586
To redirect your thinking back to who He truly is.

451
01:10:01.586 --> 01:10:08.586
Verse 14, as they traveled, they spoke with each other about everything that had happened.

452
01:10:08.586 --> 01:10:14.586
While they were talking about this, Jesus himself came up and walked along with them.

453
01:10:14.586 --> 01:10:19.586
He walked with them.

454
01:10:19.586 --> 01:10:23.586
He walks with you.

455
01:10:23.586 --> 01:10:26.586
He always walks with you.

456
01:10:26.586 --> 01:10:28.586
In your pain.

457
01:10:28.586 --> 01:10:30.586
In your sorrow.

458
01:10:30.586 --> 01:10:32.586
In your joy.

459
01:10:32.586 --> 01:10:35.586
In your sin.

460
01:10:35.586 --> 01:10:38.586
He stands above your sin.

461
01:10:38.586 --> 01:10:41.586
He stands above your uncleanness.

462
01:10:41.586 --> 01:10:46.586
He stands above your faulty thinking.

463
01:10:46.586 --> 01:10:49.586
He stands above it, for that is why He died.

464
01:10:49.586 --> 01:10:51.586
And the devil thought, now I've got Him.

465
01:10:51.586 --> 01:10:54.586
But Jesus knew, now I've got Him.

466
01:10:54.586 --> 01:10:57.586
For I am righteous and I rise from the dead.

467
01:10:57.586 --> 01:11:00.586
So now I am also king over everything the devil thought he had.

468
01:11:00.586 --> 01:11:02.586
Namely your and my sin.

469
01:11:02.586 --> 01:11:04.586
Glory to the king.

470
01:11:08.586 --> 01:11:09.586
He walked with them.

471
01:11:09.586 --> 01:11:13.586
But it was as if something was wrong with their eyes.

472
01:11:13.586 --> 01:11:16.586
For they did not recognize Him.

473
01:11:16.586 --> 01:11:19.586
Every Christian who has been in this church for two years now,

474
01:11:19.586 --> 01:11:22.586
is starting to ring bells about what this means.

475
01:11:22.586 --> 01:11:25.586
For two years ago we read from the book of Isaiah.

476
01:11:25.586 --> 01:11:27.586
As the theme for an entire year.

477
01:11:27.586 --> 01:11:30.586
To the point of annoyance, we read that chapter aloud.

478
01:11:30.586 --> 01:11:33.586
Where God says to Isaiah.

479
01:11:33.586 --> 01:11:37.586
Go tell something, but they will look, but they will not see.

480
01:11:37.586 --> 01:11:41.586
And the theme of being able to look with eyes but not see.

481
01:11:41.586 --> 01:11:44.586
Jesus repeats this in various places in the gospels.

482
01:11:44.586 --> 01:11:48.586
The concept of looking but not seeing is a very well-known concept.

483
01:11:49.586 --> 01:11:52.586
In the spiritual world for Jews and Christians.

484
01:11:52.586 --> 01:11:55.586
They all understand that if you look but do not see.

485
01:11:55.586 --> 01:12:01.586
It always has to do with not seeing the true plan of God.

486
01:12:01.586 --> 01:12:02.586
And that can come from doubt.

487
01:12:02.586 --> 01:12:04.586
That can come from sin.

488
01:12:04.586 --> 01:12:05.586
That can come from walking away.

489
01:12:05.586 --> 01:12:08.586
That can come from a hard heart.

490
01:12:08.586 --> 01:12:11.586
But we need to start thinking anew.

491
01:12:11.586 --> 01:12:13.586
We need to start thinking differently.

492
01:12:13.586 --> 01:12:18.586
This story is not a story for the crucifixion.

493
01:12:18.586 --> 01:12:24.586
I can imagine that the disciples were very disappointed on that night.

494
01:12:24.586 --> 01:12:28.586
That Jesus is there in the garden of Gethsemane crying.

495
01:12:28.586 --> 01:12:31.586
And perhaps the disciples could look at Jesus and thought to themselves.

496
01:12:31.586 --> 01:12:32.586
Oh, He is good.

497
01:12:32.586 --> 01:12:36.586
And He is crying and sweating blood and He is afraid and He says.

498
01:12:36.586 --> 01:12:40.586
Lord, if it is at all possible, please take this cup away from me.

499
01:12:40.586 --> 01:12:42.586
But not my will, but Your will be done.

500
01:12:42.586 --> 01:12:46.586
I can imagine that if you had been one of Jesus' friends.

501
01:12:46.586 --> 01:12:48.586
That you thought to yourself.

502
01:12:48.586 --> 01:12:51.586
I had different expectations.

503
01:12:51.586 --> 01:12:54.586
But this is after the cross.

504
01:12:54.586 --> 01:12:58.586
This is during the resurrection.

505
01:12:58.586 --> 01:13:00.586
Right?

506
01:13:00.586 --> 01:13:02.586
This is a resurrection story.

507
01:13:02.586 --> 01:13:08.586
And still within a resurrection story, you see that people still don't fully understand it.

508
01:13:08.586 --> 01:13:11.586
Women have already experienced his resurrection.

509
01:13:12.586 --> 01:13:14.586
And they still don't understand it.

510
01:13:14.586 --> 01:13:17.586
And here is where the bell starts to ring.

511
01:13:17.586 --> 01:13:19.586
That Jesus says.

512
01:13:19.586 --> 01:13:23.586
People may be able to look.

513
01:13:23.586 --> 01:13:25.586
But they will not see it yet.

514
01:13:25.586 --> 01:13:27.586
People may be able to hear.

515
01:13:27.586 --> 01:13:29.586
But they will not understand it.

516
01:13:29.586 --> 01:13:31.586
The concept that is explained here.

517
01:13:31.586 --> 01:13:34.586
Is expectation versus reality.

518
01:13:34.586 --> 01:13:37.586
Oh, and this is a difficult subject.

519
01:13:37.586 --> 01:13:39.586
For the believers.

520
01:13:39.586 --> 01:13:41.586
Even today.

521
01:13:41.586 --> 01:13:45.586
Expectation about what God does.

522
01:13:45.586 --> 01:13:49.586
In relation to what God truly does.

523
01:13:49.586 --> 01:13:53.586
Expectation of who God is.

524
01:13:53.586 --> 01:13:59.586
In relation to who God really is.

525
01:13:59.586 --> 01:14:01.586
